@startuml
title CFS-based delivery via E2E Service Management and NaaS approach

participant "ProductOrderDelivery\nOrchestration&Management" as PODOM
participant "E2E SM Domain\nServiceOrderManagement" as E2ESOM #blue
participant "Fixed Access Domain\nServiceOrderManagement" as FASOM #blue
participant "Network Service Domain\nServiceOrderManagement" as NSSOM #blue
participant "Soft Service Domain\nServiceOrderManagement" as SSSOM #blue
participant "EventBus" as Bus #grey

PODOM -> E2ESOM : 1 **POST Service Order TMF641**\n**E2E Connectivity Service**
activate E2ESOM
E2ESOM -> E2ESOM : 2 Validate the\nincoming request
E2ESOM --> PODOM : 3 201 Service Order created

E2ESOM -> E2ESOM : 4 Service Order Progression
note right of E2ESOM
  Depending on the
  input received for
  **E2E Connectivity Service**
  either **Fixed Fibre Access**  OR
  **Copper Access**
  will be created
end note

group Access Service

    E2ESOM -> FASOM : 5 **POST Service Order TMF641**\n**Fixed Fibre Access**
    activate FASOM
    FASOM -> FASOM : 6 Validate the\nincoming request
    FASOM --> E2ESOM : 7 201 Service Order created

    FASOM -> Bus : 8 **TMF688 Event** - Service Order Create Event
    Bus --> E2ESOM : 9 Service Order Create Event

    FASOM -> FASOM : 10 Service Order Progression
    FASOM -> Bus : 11 **TMF688 Event** - Service Order State Change Event (state=completed)
    Bus --> E2ESOM : 12 Service Order State Change Event (state=completed)

    FASOM -> Bus : 13 **TMF688 Event** - Service Create Event
    Bus --> E2ESOM : 14 Service Create Event
    deactivate FASOM

end

group Internet Service

    E2ESOM -> NSSOM : 15 **POST Service Order TMF641**\n**Fix Connectivity**
    activate NSSOM
    note right of E2ESOM : Can be via TMF640 as well and depends on implementation

    NSSOM -> NSSOM : 16 Validate the\nincoming request
    NSSOM --> E2ESOM : 17 201 Service Order created

    NSSOM -> Bus : 18 **TMF688 Event** - Service Order Create Event
    Bus --> E2ESOM : 19 Service Order Create Event

    NSSOM -> NSSOM : 20 Service Order Progression
    NSSOM -> Bus : 21 **TMF688 Event** - Service Order State Change Event (state=completed)
    Bus --> E2ESOM : 22 Service Order State Change Event (state=completed)

    NSSOM -> Bus : 23 **TMF688 Event** - Service Create Event
    Bus --> E2ESOM : 24 Service Create Event
    deactivate NSSOM

end

E2ESOM -> Bus : 25 **TMF688 Event** - Service Order State Change Event (state=completed)
E2ESOM -> Bus : 26 **TMF688 Event** - Service Create Event
deactivate E2ESOM
Bus --> PODOM : 27 Order Flow Listener

group TV Service

    PODOM -> SSSOM : 28 **POST Activation & Configuration TMF640**\n**TV Channels**
    activate SSSOM
    note right of PODOM : Can be via TMF641 as well and depends on implementation

    SSSOM -> SSSOM : 29 Validate the\nincoming request
    SSSOM -> SSSOM : 30 Service Activation\nProgression
    SSSOM --> PODOM : 31 201 Service Activated

    SSSOM -> Bus : 32 **TMF688 Event** - Service Create Event
    deactivate SSSOM

end

@enduml
